# Run outputs and data are never committed (ADR 0002). Receipts for public
# data live in receipts/public/; everything private lives under DATA_ROOT.
runs/
data/
cache/
# Logs of runs and tools (they quote frames, tracks and paths of the material they ran on)
*.log

# Restricted material (ADR 0002 section 4): NDA case files, manual labels, plugin job
# directories (<task>-<16 hex digits>), identity overrides and raw plugin outputs, also
# renamed or copied (identity_overrides (1).json, Copy of detections.jsonl,
# ball_raw2.jsonl). The directories hide everything below them, at any depth. Names that
# contain identity_override, detections or ball_raw (- and _ alike) are hidden with a
# data suffix (.json; .json[5cl]: .jsonl, .json5, .jsonc; .[nl]djson: .ndjson, .ldjson;
# .geojson; .[ct]sv: .csv, .tsv; YAML, TOML, text and XML; the arrays and tables
# .np[yz], .parquet, .feather, .arrow, .h5, .hdf5), as compressed copies (.gz, .zst,
# .bz2, .xz) and as backups (.bak, .orig, .old, .backup, .tmp, .save, ~); the other
# names with the suffixes they are written with. No pattern ends like code or
# documentation (.py, .pyi, .md, .rst), so identity_overrides.py and detections.md stay
# visible without a negation: a negation would also re-include what a developer
# excluded in .git/info/exclude or a global excludes file, since .gitignore takes
# precedence over both. The gate's restricted_data check (G4) fails on these names when
# they are force-added, and on what these patterns leave visible to git add -A
# (src/gbf/gate/datafiles.py): identity_override, detections and ball_raw names with any
# other suffix except code and documentation, such as a figure (detections-overview.svg),
# a spreadsheet or database (.xlsx, .sqlite), an archive or another compressor (.zip,
# .7z, .br), a numbered or partial copy (.jsonl.1, .part), an editor or lock file (.swp,
# .~lock.*#) or a name without a suffix, and hand labels under another JSON name, which
# it recognises by their content. A directory named like such material with a backup
# suffix (detections.old/) is hidden with everything below it, code and docs included.
cases/
labels/
label/
manual[-_]label/
manual[-_]labels*/
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]/
*identity[-_]override*.json
*identity[-_]override*.json[5cl]
*identity[-_]override*.[nl]djson
*identity[-_]override*.geojson
*identity[-_]override*.[ct]sv
*identity[-_]override*.yaml
